{"ts":"2026-08-16T10:52:26.636Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"736bc2ce37b57aa429143ced","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"release-operator","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-f6zjpq","release:pm-suhxny"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-f6zjpq","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-f6zjpq","release:pm-suhxny"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.233","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-16T10:52:26.636Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Coverage before and after, measured against docs/generated/AGENT_COMMAND_SURFACE.md (75 commands: 13 core, 22 standard, 36 full plus 4 internal).\n\nBefore, no skill named an entry point for four capability families: relationships (graph, deps), declared invariants (assurance, validate as a gate rather than a check), branch and fleet (merge, claim/release as concurrency primitives), and the entire read-output budget surface (--output-budget, --output-limit, --output-include, --output-cursor, --output-session, --output-format, --token-accounting). The last is the surface whose sole purpose is keeping an agent's context small, and it appeared in zero of twelve skill bundles.\n\nAlso absent from every bundle: the never-pass---author rule, despite it being an AGENTS.md non-negotiable and a user mandate.\n\nAfter: pm guide returns 12 topics (was 8). The four new topics - tokens, graph, assurance, merge - each carry commands, two workflow templates, and doc references verified to exist. Each of the four canonical SKILL.md files declares a load order with measured per-tier costs and a capability map naming an entry command and a guide topic per family. Eight harness plugin skills carry the same token-discipline and guide-routing block.\n\nMeasured routing costs now stated in the skills rather than implied: SKILL.md ~650 tok, pm guide <topic> --depth brief ~640 tok, pm list-open --limit 20 ~909 tok, pm context --limit 10 ~2,063 tok, pm next ~2,525 tok, pm contracts --summary ~2,637 tok, pm help ~3,136 tok, pm contracts --command list --flags-only ~3,372 tok, pm guide commands --depth standard ~7,981 tok, docs/COMMANDS.md ~28,980 tok, docs/SDK.md ~45,117 tok. Both large documents are now routed into by heading rather than linked whole; SURFACE_MAP.md and AUTHORING.md carry the heading indexes.\n\nGate: validateSkillReferenceReachability fails when a references/*.md is not linked from its own SKILL.md. Negative control proven - an unlinked ORPHAN.md fails naming the exact path, removing it restores the pass. The gate already runs in CI via docs.yml and release.yml.\n\nVerification: docs/skills gate passed, Claude plugin smoke passed, full test suite passed, pnpm quality:static passed."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-16T10:52:26.636Z"}],"before_hash":"f7e4fe3728b9839d45b521957378c60c760058531feaa7f814b6b3dbf59b23ec","after_hash":"bf6c8de33a76bd5b1ab6d902acc28bd152fb3c75b7fab9636fe748eb811a95ed","item_hash_version":2}
